WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:11.149
"Come and get it!" called Cookie.

2
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:16.110
Frank and the other cowboys came up to Cookie's wagon.

3
00:00:16.111 --> 00:00:23.375
The children served the hungry men and everyone sat around a big fire to eat.

4
00:00:23.376 --> 00:00:28.462
"Frank says you can stay," Cookie said to Vinnie and Mandy.

5
00:00:28.463 --> 00:00:31.783
"But you'd better keep out of trouble."

6
00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:36.506
"We promise!" exclaimed the children.

7
00:00:36.507 --> 00:00:41.592
Mandy listened to the cowboys tell stories, and said,

8
00:00:41.593 --> 00:00:45.827
"I wish I had a cowboy hat and boots."

9
00:00:45.828 --> 00:00:50.414
"I wish I had a gun!" Vinnie cried.

10
00:00:50.415 --> 00:00:54.592
"Hey, kids," a cowboy called out.

11
00:00:54.593 --> 00:00:57.495
He held up a harmonica.

12
00:00:57.496 --> 00:00:59.816
"Sing something."

13
00:00:59.817 --> 00:01:04.187
"I can't sing," said Vinnie shyly.

14
00:01:04.188 --> 00:01:10.142
"He's right! He can't sing!" giggled Mandy.

15
00:01:10.143 --> 00:01:13.712
"Come on," the cowboy said.

16
00:01:13.713 --> 00:01:17.935
"Singing calms the cattle, so they can sleep."

17
00:01:17.936 --> 00:01:21.562
"Like a lullaby?" asked Vinnie.

18
00:01:21.563 --> 00:01:25.383
"Yep. We all sing, so don't be shy,"

19
00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:30.229
said the cowboy, and he began to play.

20
00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:36.052
"Oh, give me a home where the buffalo roam,"

21
00:01:36.053 --> 00:01:40.928
sang Vinnie as the cattle mooed happily.

22
00:01:40.929 --> 00:01:45.345
Meanwhile, Mandy was helping Cookie clean up.

23
00:01:45.346 --> 00:01:49.442
"What is the Chisholm Trail?" she asked.

24
00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:54.520
"Well, we take the cattle from Texas along the trail to Kansas.

25
00:01:54.521 --> 00:02:00.607
The cattle end up at the market where they are sold," explained Cookie.

26
00:02:00.608 --> 00:02:04.672
"How long does it take?" asked Mandy.

27
00:02:04.673 --> 00:02:09.060
"Depends on the weather and the Indians," said Cookie.

28
00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:12.535
"It can take from two to three months."

29
00:02:12.536 --> 00:02:18.573
Later some cowboys unrolled their beds and went to sleep.

30
00:02:18.574 --> 00:02:27.114
Others just leaned back, covered their eyes with their hats, and slept on the ground.

31
00:02:27.115 --> 00:02:32.378
Cookie gave Mandy and Vinnie bedrolls. Vinnie yawned.

32
00:02:32.379 --> 00:02:37.470
A few men were walking around, staring at the herd.

33
00:02:37.471 --> 00:02:42.066
"Why aren't those men sleeping?" Vinnie asked Frank.

34
00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:46.217
"They're guarding the cattle," Frank replied.

35
00:02:46.218 --> 00:02:49.369
"From what?" asked Mandy.

36
00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:54.867
"Wild animals, cattle thieves, and Indians," said Frank.

37
00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:58.639
The children heard howling in the distance.

38
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.103
Mandy moved closer to her brother.

39
00:03:02.104 --> 00:03:07.379
The next morning, the children woke to a sunny day.

40
00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:11.277
Everyone was already up and ready to go.

41
00:03:11.278 --> 00:03:17.283
The wagon was loaded, and the cattle were starting to move again.

42
00:03:17.284 --> 00:03:20.925
"Good morning, kids," Cookie called.

43
00:03:20.926 --> 00:03:26.072
"You missed breakfast, but I saved you some biscuits.

44
00:03:26.073 --> 00:03:28.132
We have to get going."

45
00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:32.605
"Where?" asked Vinnie, munching on his biscuit.

46
00:03:32.606 --> 00:03:35.542
"It's time to get back on the trail,"

47
00:03:35.543 --> 00:03:40.913
said Frank as he brought over Vinnie's horse from the previous day.

48
00:03:40.914 --> 00:03:44.034
The horse sniffed Vinnie's biscuit.

49
00:03:44.035 --> 00:03:47.389
"You come with me."

50
00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:51.546
"And Mandy can ride with me," said Cookie.

51
00:03:51.547 --> 00:03:55.970
He picked her up and helped her climb onto the wagon seat.

52
00:03:55.971 --> 00:04:00.228
The horses followed the cattle at an easy pace.

53
00:04:00.229 --> 00:04:04.805
They rode over dry, flat prairies of tall grass.

54
00:04:04.806 --> 00:04:09.683
The sun was hot, and the sky was bright blue.

55
00:04:09.684 --> 00:04:12.348
There was a soft wind.

56
00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:17.517
Vinnie wiped his face with his sleeve and thought:

57
00:04:17.518 --> 00:04:24.055
"This is the life of a cowboy!"
